<title>USA: Attractive rates push U.S. debt issuers to finance.</title>
<headline>Attractive rates push U.S. debt issuers to finance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. corporations continue to tap the corporate bond primary market as attractive interest rates lure issuers to finance debt now, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There are a lot of names being kicked around but we haven't heard anything official yet,&quot; said one syndicate source. &quot;With rates at such attractive levels we should certainly see more issuance.&quot;</p>
<p>Currently, IBM Corp is rumored to bring between $500 and $600 million of a 100-year bond via Salomon Brothers, syndicate sources said. Price talk on the issue is seen in the high 70 basis points arena, they added.</p>
